# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing in this project needs credentials today — the controller integration
# that did is dropped — but the guard stays, because the cost of it being here
# and unnecessary is nothing and the cost of it being absent once is permanent.
.env
*.pem
*.p12

# ── Swift and SwiftPM ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.doccarchive

# Package.resolved is committed: the app resolves zhen-core by a version range, and the lock
# file is what pins the exact release (AGENTS.md: pinned to a version, never a branch). It
# lives in Zhen.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/.

# ── Xcode ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zhen.xcodeproj is Xcode's (folder-synchronised groups) and IS committed.
# Per-user state and build products are not.
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
# A workspace at the root would be a second container; the project's own is committed.
/*.xcworkspace

# ── Build products ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/

# Rasterised icons at the repository root. Design/marks/03-z/ is the source; a
# checked-in PNG at the root is a second answer to the question "what does the mark
# look like", and it is the one that goes stale without anybody noticing.
/icon-*.png


# ── macOS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store


